    {
      "title": "API Versioning: URI vs Header",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "API Versioning: URI vs Header",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Where the Version Lives",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "URI",
                "Header",
                "Query"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Form",
                  "`/v1/orders`, `/v2/orders`",
                  "`Accept` media type or `X-API-Version`",
                  "`?version=2`"
                ],
                [
                  "Strength",
                  "Visible, cacheable, curl-friendly",
                  "Clean URLs",
                  "Simple"
                ],
                [
                  "Catch",
                  "URLs proliferate",
                  "Hidden, hard in a browser",
                  "Easy to omit"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "GET /v2/orders",
                "Accept: application/vnd.acme.v2+json",
                "X-API-Version: 2",
                "GET /orders?version=2"
              ],
              "note": "URI, media type, custom header, query"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Trade-offs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "URI: easy to route and test, but the version is ==not part of the resource identity==",
                "Header: caches must ==Vary== on that header",
                "Query: always define a ==default version== when the client sends none"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Policy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Version only on ==breaking== changes, not every release",
                "Prefer **additive** changes so most clients never move",
                "Pick ==one scheme== per API and apply it consistently",
                "Cap supported versions, e.g. ==N and N-1=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Cost of side by side",
              "text": "Running v1 and v2 together **doubles maintenance**. Cap how many versions live at once."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Schema Evolution for Events: Avro, Protobuf, Registry",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Schema Evolution for Events: Avro, Protobuf, Registry",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Registry and Modes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Registry stores ==versioned schemas== per **subject**, e.g. `orders-value`",
                "Messages carry only a ==schema ID==",
                "Registry **rejects** a schema that breaks the subject's mode"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Reads",
                "Upgrade first"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "BACKWARD (default)",
                  "new reads old",
                  "consumers"
                ],
                [
                  "FORWARD",
                  "old reads new",
                  "producers"
                ],
                [
                  "FULL",
                  "both",
                  "any order"
                ],
                [
                  "`_TRANSITIVE`",
                  "all versions, not latest",
                  "same as base"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Avro",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reader and writer schemas ==resolved at read time==",
                "Added field needs a ==default== (backward)",
                "Only fields **with defaults** may be removed",
                "Rename needs ==aliases==",
                "No field numbers: schema must be present at read time, hence the registry"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Protobuf",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Identity = ==field number==, never the name",
                "Never reuse or renumber; mark removed ones `reserved`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "protobuf",
              "lines": [
                "reserved 4;",
                "reserved \"old_name\";"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "New fields default to zero, so ==absence is ambiguous==",
                "No `required` in proto3; unknown fields kept or ignored"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rollout order",
              "text": "BACKWARD: upgrade consumers first. FORWARD: upgrade producers first."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Deprecation, Tolerant Reader and Expand-Contract",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Deprecation, Tolerant Reader and Expand-Contract",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Tolerant Reader",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Postel: be liberal in what you accept",
                "==Ignore unknown fields==; read only what you need",
                "Do not fail on **new enum values** or extra JSON properties",
                "Main enabler of {green:forward compatibility}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Deprecation Workflow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Announce** it; set `deprecated: true` in OpenAPI",
                "Send `Deprecation` and `Sunset` headers",
                "Monitor ==per-client usage==",
                "Remove only when usage hits {red:zero}"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Deprecation: @1767225600",
                "Sunset: Thu, 31 Dec 2026 23:59:59 GMT"
              ],
              "note": "RFC 9745: unix seconds; Sunset is an HTTP date"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Expand and Contract",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Rename old_name to new_name",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "1 Expand",
                    "note": "R1: add new_name, write both",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2 Migrate",
                    "note": "R2: switch readers one by one",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3 Contract",
                    "note": "R3: stop writing old_name; R4: delete it",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Catch Breaks in CI",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Contract tests (Pact): consumer expectations",
                "`buf breaking` for Protobuf",
                "Registry compatibility API for Avro",
                "Fail the build before merge"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
